{"run_id": "monday-004__glm5.2__005", "kind": "criterion", "criterion_id": "figures_carried_correctly", "result": "PARTIAL", "evidence": "Segment table: Mid-market total ARR EUR 1,510,000 and SMB EUR 572,800, against EUR 1,710,000 and EUR 602,400 in customers.csv (active bases are EUR 1,530,000 and EUR 478,800, so neither reading fits); the derived averages EUR 151,000 and EUR 31,822 inherit the error. The plan comparison row mixes bases: 'Churn risk: Low (0%) | Moderate (11%) | Severe (43%)' sets Pro's logo churn beside Starter's MRR churn.", "reason": "Two wrong figures from one source - the segment ARR column - plus the averages derived from them, and one unlabelled change of basis. None is decision-changing: the SMB argument runs on 4 of 18, EUR 10,300/month and the EUR 792 Starter margin, all exact. Everything else checkable is exact, and there is a great deal of it - the full plan P&L for both months, all six margins, contribution per customer, the funnel table reconciling to 1,000/100 and 1,500/120, the new-logo and expansion splits, revenue per trial and per lead, Acme's tokens-per-request walk, Stark and Wayne against their allowances, the MRR bridge to EUR 732,400 and the 96.7% NRR approximation."}
